// SPDX-License-Identifier: Apache-2.0
; specs/widgets/vcd-wrapped.t27 -- your simulation, wrapped: a summary card for a VCD file
; Source of truth for public/widgets/vcd-wrapped/ (gHashTag/trinity, apps/website). The page is
; written by scripts/widget-pages-from-spec.mjs from this file; tool.js holds no English of its
; own and reads every word below from window.T27_WIDGET.
; ASCII only (L3), English only (LANG-EN).

; WHAT IT DOES: the reader drops a .vcd file (IEEE 1364 value change dump, from iverilog/vvp,
; Verilator, GHDL or any simulator that writes one). The page reads it in the browser with
; public/widgets/vcd-wrapped/vcdstats.js, streaming the file in chunks so a large dump is read in
; the memory of its signal list, never its waveform. It shows one card: the value changes and bit
; flips in the whole run, the busiest nets, the quietest nets, the signals that never leave X or Z,
; the signals that end in X or Z, the simulated time span, and how many signals and scopes the dump
; declares. The card can be saved as a 1200x630 PNG drawn in the page. The file never leaves the
; browser. It is a summary, not a viewer: the test-waves widget draws waveforms.

; HOW IT COUNTS: a value change is a recorded value that differs from the signal's previous value;
; the first value a signal gets (usually from $dumpvars) is its start, not a change. Bit flips count
; the bit positions that differ between the two values. One id code declared in several scopes is
; one signal with several names. A signal stays X/Z when none of its values is fully known.
; Parameters are constants and are counted apart. Values inside $dumpoff are skipped.

; THE SAMPLES: three real Icarus Verilog 12.0 runs, made one at a time by
; scripts/widget-data/vcd-wrapped.mjs. "counter" is specs/ternary/clocked_counter.t27 compiled to
; Verilog by public/t27/t27_compiler.wasm in node and driven by a hand-written testbench,
; scripts/widget-data/vcd-wrapped-counter-tb.v (not generated from the spec). "vsa-bind" and "tmu"
; are RTL committed under fpga/openxc7-synth/ with their own committed testbenches, run as they
; are. The tmu testbench fails all its tests in this repository: tmu.v reads tmu_test_w_wide.mem
; and no such file is committed, so its outputs stay X; it is shipped because that is what a real
; broken run looks like. Each VCD is shipped as vvp dumped it, not trimmed: all are under
; K_MAX_SAMPLE_BYTES. Every K_ fact below is re-read from the shipped VCDs by
; `node scripts/widget-data/vcd-wrapped.mjs --check`.

; WHAT IT DOES NOT CLAIM: that a busy net is a bug, or that a quiet one is fine. A signal stuck at
; X is often a real fault (an unloaded memory, a missing reset) and sometimes harmless (the locals
; of a function never called). The card counts what the dump recorded; a signal the testbench did
; not $dumpvars is not in it. It does not run a simulation.
; phi^2 + 1/phi^2 = 3 | TRINITY

